--[[
	Vfx: every particle effect as data (art/vfx/CATALOGUE.md). Built on the client by Visuals/Vfx;
	the sprite ids live in Config/VfxSprites (generated; a sprite not uploaded yet skips its emitter).

	An effect is a list of emitter specs. Spec keys (anything else is rejected by Vfx.spec):
	  sprite         a name in Vfx.Sprites (art/vfx/SPRITES.md)
	  grey           true: the sprite's tintable grey twin, coloured by `color` (TINT sprites only)
	  color          "#RRGGBB" or ColorSequence keys { { t, "#RRGGBB" }, ... } (default white)
	  useColor       bursts: opts.color (a Color3) replaces `color` when given (hatch rarity)
	  rate           particles per second (persistent effects)   emit   burst count (bursts)
	  lifetime       { min, max } seconds
	  size           studs, a number or NumberSequence keys { { t, v }, ... }
	  transparency   NumberSequence keys (default FADE: in fast, out slow)
	  speed          number or { min, max }     spread   number or { x, y } degrees
	  accel          { x, y, z }                drag     number
	  rot, rotSpeed  { min, max } degrees (per second)
	  lightEmission  0.15 - 0.3 in daylight (0.8 - 1 washes every sprite to white on the sunny sky);
	                 above that only with core = true (portal cores)
	  lightInfluence 0 - 1 (default 0.3)
	  orientation    "FacingCamera" | "FacingCameraWorldUp" | "VelocityParallel" | "VelocityPerpendicular"
	                 (VelocityPerpendicular + a tiny speed lays a sprite flat: runes, rings, ground glow)
	  direction      emission direction, a NormalId name (default "Top")
	  shape, shapeStyle, shapeInOut   emitter shape (only where the emitter sits on a part: a
	                 monster's "body" volume, a landmark box, a burst box)
	  zOffset        studs towards the camera (lifts bursts out of meshes)
	  lockedToPart   particles follow the monster
	  at             monsters: "feet" | "core" | "head" | "body" (body = a volume round the body);
	                 hovering body types (moth, sprite) turn "feet" into "core".
	                 landmarks: { x, y, z } as fractions of the box round the building's visible
	                 parts (its 3D mesh once dressed), in Body's orientation (front is -Z, y = -0.5
	                 is the floor); the Sky Gate is measured the same way (its Gate model has a Body).
	  offset         monsters: { x, y, z } studs added to the anchor (scaled like sizes)
	  box            landmarks and bursts: { x, y, z } studs, the part the particles spawn in
	  core           a portal core: may glow above 0.3 (landmarks only)
	  night          0..1: how much this emitter glows at night (default: its sprite's Night.sprites
	                 weight; 0 keeps it as lit by day, which is right for smoke, dust and leaves)

	Monster numbers are authored for a monster RefHeight studs tall; Visuals/Vfx scales sizes,
	speeds, accelerations and offsets with the model's Height. Budgets (live particles =
	rate x lifetime max): an aura <= 8, an aura with two mutations <= 12, a landmark <= 60.

	Night: the daytime LightEmission rule (<= 0.3) is about the sunny sky washing glows out. After
	dark the same sprites look dull and, with LightInfluence > 0, go grey with the world, so Night
	lifts glowing sprites: LightEmission + boost x weight x night (up to cap) and LightInfluence
	x (1 - weight x night). `night` (0..1) follows Lighting.ClockTime through dusk and dawn.

	Tables: Auras[element], Mutations[mutationId], Variants.shiny / .rainbow, Rarity[rarityId],
	Landmarks[hubId | "skyGate"], Bursts[name], Night, Eggs[eggId], EggReady, Mastery[key] (3.3: a
	monster's mastery aura, appearance.aura; Gold / Mythic lines and the Star Shard auras;
	<= Budget.mastery each).

	Eggs use the monster keys (at = feet / core / head / body, measured on the shell), authored for
	an egg EggRefHeight studs tall (the incubator's); Visuals/Vfx scales them with the egg's height.
]]

